From b6fa5efcf962da0d7013ff9fe7bc1ef7c5350280 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: konkanello <konkanello@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:39:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mimicos: let MimicOS own memory management

ChampSim invents its own physical addresses: frames come off a shuffled
free list and page-table pages are made up as the walker needs them.
That is fine as a placeholder, but it means physical placement -- the
thing an OS allocator decides -- is not modelled, and a page fault is a
fixed number of cycles that says nothing about what a handler does.

This hands all of it to MimicOS.  Opt-in and inert by default:

  make MIMICOS_HOME=/path/to/mimicos
  MIMICOS_CONFIG=<mimicos.ini> bin/champsim ...

Without MIMICOS_HOME, src/vmem_mimicos.cc compiles to stubs, nothing
links against MimicOS, and behaviour is identical to stock.

What it adds:

  Allocation and page tables.  va_to_pa() and get_pte_pa() ask MimicOS.
  Since the entries have real physical addresses, the existing page
  table walker fetches them through the cache hierarchy, so allocator
  policy shows up in measured traffic instead of being assumed away.

  Two page sizes in the TLBs.  A TLB is indexed on the page number, so
  an entry for a 2M page cannot be found by a lookup that indexes on
  the 4K page number; every lookup now probes twice and entries record
  which they are.  Separate arrays for an L1, shared capacity for an
  L2, both configured per TLB.  Off by default.

  The fault handler, for real.  ChampSim cannot execute code, so point
  MIMICOS_FAULT_TRACE at a recording of MimicOS servicing a fault and
  those instructions are replayed into the core at each fault.  They
  fetch, decode and execute like any others.  A 4K fault is 565
  instructions; promoting to 2M is 1426.

  Kernel instructions are marked, so they do not count towards the
  program's IPC, and their accesses skip address translation entirely:
  MimicOS is what answers a translation and cannot translate for
  itself.

  --deadlock-cycle.  A measured minor fault is microseconds, thousands
  of cycles, and the hardcoded 500-cycle window reported that as a
  deadlock.  Default unchanged.

Measured on 605.mcf, 1M instructions after 200k warmup, fault cost held
fixed so only placement differs:

  stock (shuffled free list)   IPC 0.1001   LLC misses 116552
  MimicOS, baseline allocator  IPC 0.1597   LLC misses  89201

and with page size varying, 150k instructions:

  4K     IPC 0.01324   DTLB miss 29650   STLB miss 3650
  2M     IPC 0.08224   DTLB miss  5654   STLB miss  342

The full suite passes: 10894 assertions over 626 cases, including new
tests for the MimicOS paths.  A stock build passes 10842 over 622,
unchanged.

